<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Geronimo is a man of 77 with chronic post-traumatic stress disorder and moderate alcohol use disorder who comes for his first annual wellness visit, two weeks after his eleven-week review. He has finished ten of twelve sessions of cognitive processing therapy and takes sertraline 50 mg and naltrexone 50 mg daily. His cough from the chest cold five weeks ago is gone. Nightmares come about twice a week, down from most nights, and he has had one evening of heavy drinking since his last visit. He has not fallen. He cannot recall any vaccines or screening tests as an adult and wants the ones that will help him at his age. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Initial annual wellness visit, age 77</td></tr><tr><td>PTSD</td><td>Ten of twelve therapy sessions; nightmares about twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>One evening of heavy drinking in two weeks; otherwise one drink or none</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 1</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Sertraline 50 mg, naltrexone 50 mg, thiamine 100 mg daily</td></tr><tr><td>Cognition</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Asked aloud with the clinic&apos;s Apache interpreter, at his choice, and reviewed with him by Dr. Whitehorse-Lindgren. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Fair, better than in the summer</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Lives alone on the military reservation among his people; sees friends most days; the restrictions on travel weigh on him</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>In treatment; one evening of heavy drinking in two weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>No commercial tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Rides and works with his cattle most days; balance exercises three times a week</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Eats two meals a day; beef, corn and beans; less at night since he drinks less</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Six hours most nights; nightmares about twice a week</td></tr><tr><td>Safety at home</td><td>Feels safe at home; a light now on the path to his door</td></tr><tr><td>Falls</td><td>One fall three months ago; none since</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent in all activities and instrumental activities of daily living</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>Hears well in quiet rooms; sees well at a distance, needs light for close work</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
