    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Initial annual wellness visit completed</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and a written prevention plan given to him, read aloud through the interpreter. Hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening offered and done today. At 77, with no screening before, he chose a stool immunochemical test for colorectal cancer after hearing that the benefit at his age is smaller. Prostate cancer screening is not recommended at 70 and older. Statin use for primary prevention after 75 is a matter of shared decision-making; with no diabetes or high blood pressure and a wish to take no more pills now, he chose not to have a lipid test or statin today. [S]<list><item>High-dose influenza, PCV20 and RSV vaccines today.</item><item>Stool immunochemical test kit given, to return within two weeks.</item><item>Hepatitis results by phone through the interpreter.</item><item>Recombinant zoster and Tdap at the sixteen-week visit.</item><item>Next wellness visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">History of falling (Z91.81)</content>. No falls since intake; Timed Up and Go 11 seconds, from 13; no fall in standing pressure. [S]<list><item>Continue balance and strength exercises.</item><item>No drinking before riding or walking out at night.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Cognitive assessment</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Mini-Cog 5 of 5; no concern from him</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 1; PTSD in treatment</td></tr><tr><td>Falls prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Timed Up and Go 11 seconds; exercise program; no orthostatic drop</td></tr><tr><td>Functional ability and home safety</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Independent; a light on the path to his door</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Alcohol use disorder in treatment with naltrexone</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco cessation</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No commercial tobacco</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Ages 76 to 85: selective; never screened, and he chose a stool immunochemical test</td></tr><tr><td>Prostate cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Not recommended at 70 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Lung cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>No smoking history</td></tr><tr><td>Abdominal aortic aneurysm screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>Recommended for men 65 to 75 who have ever smoked; he is 77 and has not smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Statin for primary prevention</td><td>Declined</td><td>Evidence is insufficient after 75; offered a lipid test and discussion, and he chose not to now</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One-time screening for adults 18 to 79</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Triple panel, recommended once for all adults</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>High-dose vaccine, preferred at 65 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Pneumococcal vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PCV20, one dose; no earlier pneumococcal vaccine</td></tr><tr><td>RSV vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One dose, recommended for all adults 75 and older</td></tr><tr><td>Recombinant zoster vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>Two doses; first at the sixteen-week visit, at his choice of no more than three injections today</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Due</td><td>No booster he can recall; Tdap at the sixteen-week visit</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Declined</td><td>Offered for the coming season; he will decide later</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Influenza vaccine, high-dose, for the coming season (preferred at 65 and older); Pneumococcal conjugate vaccine (PCV20), one dose; no earlier pneumococcal vaccine; RSV vaccine, one dose, recommended for all adults 75 and older [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Special General Memorandum 94-08: Statement of Policy for the Traditional Cultural Advocacy Program (1994); Falls Prevention in Community-Dwelling Older Adults: Interventions (2024); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); Medicare Wellness Visits (Medicare Learning Network) (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Sixteen-week review in three weeks, with zoster and Tdap. Stool test and hepatitis results by phone. Next wellness visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-28: sixteen-week review after twelve therapy sessions: symptoms, drinking, safety and his plan. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

